    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## OWNER ORCHESTRATION RESET R02 — ROOT CAUSE + SINGLE PRODUCT STREAM\n\nCURRENT_MAIN = `b18ca6b9cce2dce6fe304ca8ae36c05df4f4dcb1`\nOWNER_ROUTE_TIME = 2026-09-02\nROOT = DUNCAN PRIME\n\n### ROOT CAUSE FOUND\nThe repeated W01/source/runtime loop was not caused by a missing character pack.\n\nIt was caused by **control-topology overgrowth**:\n1. `#248` turned six diagnostic costume-force controls into a serial hard gate before POSE/CAMERA/S001.\n2. `studio/ZORR_THREE_CHAT_ORCHESTRATION_R01.md` split one product path across CHAT A / B / C.\n3. Parallel chats accumulated different durable checkpoints/NEXT values at different times.\n4. Visual attempts existed as transient conversation artifacts that were not independently visible across chats, so integration could only consume partial durable summaries/matrices.\n5. Old locally true blockers (Library visibility, Linux runtime, source-bound editor, Krita binding) remained durable and were repeatedly rediscovered/promoted after fresher product context had already changed.\n6. Night queue #254 scheduled several layers around the same gate but has zero durable execution comments; schedule/activity did not equal product delivery.\n\nThis is exactly the class of process failure prohibited by Constitution `SIMPLEST-SUFFICIENT`, `ONE-CRITICAL-PATH`, `NO-TREADING-WATER`, `PRODUCT-FIRST`, `STOP-RULE FOR PROCESS COMPLEXITY`, and #204 `ONE ACTIVE BASE` / parallelism-only-when-independent.\n\n### W01 ROLE CORRECTION\n`W01 ARM_RAISE` is a useful **high-information diagnostic** because one shoulder elevation simultaneously tests shoulder seam, sleeve-cap/armhole, collar-lapel root, side-chest/armpit force localization, calm opposite planes, and no rubber-sheet jacket behavior.\n\nIt is **not a magical required film frame** and is no longer a universal standalone prerequisite for all downstream ZORR production.\n\nThe six #248 controls remain a reusable mechanics/QC library. Apply only the control(s) relevant to a real production pose/key drawing, or run a standalone control when a concrete regression/gap requires it.\n\n### ACTIVE TOPOLOGY — R02\n`ONE ACTIVE PRODUCT STREAM = #251 / DUNCAN PRIME MASTER`\n\n- CHAT A parallel execution topology = RETIRED.\n- CHAT B parallel execution topology = RETIRED; its completed PREP artifacts remain reusable evidence.\n- CHAT C label is retired; #251 is simply the single DUNCAN PRIME product/master stream.\n- SHERIFF remains independent monitoring/evidence control and must not become a product executor.\n- Night/automation tasks may monitor or execute only a specifically delegated bounded job and may not create their own competing ACTIVE_BASE/NEXT.\n\n### #248 AFTER RESET\n`COSTUME_MECHANICS_R01 = SUPPORTING QC / ON-DEMAND`\n`W01 = DIAGNOSTIC CONTROL / NOT UNIVERSAL HARD GATE`\n`SIX STANDALONE WITNESSES = NOT REQUIRED BEFORE UNRELATED REAL PRODUCTION POSES`\n\nRelevant costume mechanics still must pass on any actual key drawing where that force exists. This is not a waiver of quality; it moves verification onto real product artifacts instead of synthetic gate ceremony.\n\n### ACTIVE PRODUCT OBJECTIVE\n`FIRST_REAL_PRODUCTION_KEY_DRAWING / SCENE-BOUND POSE CANDIDATE`\n\nUse the locked character model (#245 PASS) and existing camera/S001 prep from #250. Produce/choose a real product key drawing or scene-bound pose candidate first; then run only the relevant identity/body/costume/pose/camera QC against that artifact.\n\nDo not invent a standalone diagnostic frame unless the real production artifact exposes a concrete mechanics gap.\n\n### RETIRE AS ACTIVE BLOCKERS\n- whole-pack rediscovery;\n- Krita binding;\n- exact MASTER FRONT direct-edit requirement;\n- Linux OpenToonz absence;\n- six synthetic costume witness frames as a prerequisite to all product work;\n- A/B/C chat coordination itself.\n\n### NEXT\n1. persist this reset into #248/#249/#250/#251 + restore entrypoint #204;\n2. mark old three-chat orchestration contract as SUPERSEDED;\n3. keep completed B prep reusable;\n4. continue from one real production artifact, not another process proof.\n\nNo PASS is claimed for a new key drawing/shot. No canon mutation. No main merge claimed.",
